===Etymology 2===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*ḱley-|id=incline}}
From {{inh|en|enm|lawe}}, from {{inh|en|ang|hlāw|t=burial mound}}. Also spelled [[low]].

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A [[tumulus]] of [[stone#Noun|stones]].
# {{lb|en|Northern England|Scotland|archaic}} A [[hill]].
#* {{RQ:Stevenson Across the Plains|part=I|page=209|passage=[Y]ou might climb the '''Law''', where the whale's jawbone stood landmark in the buzzing wind, and behold the face of many counties, and the smoke and spires of many towns, and the sails of distant ships.}}

===Etymology 3===
From {{inh|en|enm|lagh}}, from {{der|en|non|lag|t=that which is lying or laid, position, price, way, sting, blow}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*lagą|t=that which is laid}}. Cognate with {{cog|sco|lauch|t=one's tavern-reckoning or one's share of the cost, a score; a payment for drink or entertainment}}, {{cog|enm|lai|t=one's share of expenses, one's bill or account}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|dialectal|or|obsolete}} A [[score]]; [[share]] of [[expense]]; [[legal]] [[charge]].

